      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Instead of completely stopping the squat, structure the deload with significantly reduced load, perhaps using 50-60% of their working weight. Maintain the movement pattern and some frequency, but drastically cut the sets and reps to prioritize recovery over intensity. This maintains neuromuscular connection without overloading the recovering CNS, essentially providing active recovery while minimizing perceived loss of stimulus.",
      "source": "target",
