    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Got it, so it's more about keeping the mechanics sharp while letting the system reset. I guess my other concern is just that weird feeling when they hit a wall—it feels almost like they're fighting against something invisible just to get that last rep. Is there any biological reason why progress feels so stagnant or \"stuck\" sometimes, even when everything else is dialed in?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That sensation of fighting an invisible wall is often related to accumulated connective tissue fatigue or neuromuscular inefficiency, not just muscle exhaustion. The body adapts to the current stimulus, and when it plateaus, the limiting factor may shift from muscle strength to coordination or stiffness. Sometimes, insufficient recovery at a microscopic level, even with good nutrition, prevents the necessary cellular adaptations required for further strength gains.",
      "source": "target",
